      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000119763,
      "SummaryText": "PREVENTION & RESPONSE POLICY\nBidart Bros. uses a comprehensive environmental management system approach to integrate both accidental release prevention and emergency response requirements under the \"One Plan\" format.\n\nSTATIONARY SOURCE & REGULATED SUBSTANCES\nBidart Bros. Potato Packing House washes, packages potatoes for produce distribution.  One ton cylinders of chlorine are used to sanitize produce wash water.  Chlorine is utilized during the potato packing season only, and is not maintained above threshold quantities on site during the remainder of the year.  Therefore, this initial RMP submission coincides with the date on which chlorine is seasonally present in the water treatment process, at the threshold quantity, in accordance with the RMP rule.\n\nWORST CASE SCENARIO\nThe worst case toxic gas release scenario is considered to be a one ton cylinder of chlorine releasing its entire contents in ten minutes.  The worst case is not likely to occur, but is addressed in the federal regulations primarily as a baseline reference of comparative risk.  Theoretically speaking, a complete volatilization of the ton container of chlorine in ten minutes time could produce a vapor cloud of harmful concentrations which may extend over a considerable distance.  If such release were to occur, there could be residential populations (depending on wind direction) and industrial sites affected.  \n\nALTERNATIVE RELEASE SCENARIO\nThe worst case toxic gas release scenario is considered to be a one ton cylinder of chlorine releasing its entire contents in ten minutes.  The worst case is not likely to occur, but is addressed in the federal regulations primarily as a baseline reference of comparative risk.  Theoretically speaking, a complete volatilization of the ton container of chlorine in ten minutes time could produce a vapor cloud of harmful concentrations which may extend over a considerable distance.  If such release were to occur, there could be residential populations (depending on"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000119763,
      "SummaryText": "wind direction) and industrial sites affected.  \n\nACCIDENTAL RELEASE PREVENTION PROGRAM:\nBidart Bros. has integrated the California Accidental Release Program (CalARP) requirements within a comprehensive environmental management system based on the \"One Plan\" format.\n\nFIVE YEAR ACCIDENT HISTORY:\nBidart Bros. has not had an accidental release of a regulated substance during the past five years.\n\nEMERGENCY RESPONSE PROGRAM:\nBidart Bros. uses a comprehensive environmental management system approach to integrate both accidental release prevention and emergency response requirements.\n\nPLANNED CHANGES TO IMPROVE SAFETY:\nNo plans at this time"
    }
  ]
